silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_04_commuting_square_sentence_chain_sections_04_inconsistency_as_non_commuting_concrete_anchor_2_chain_bottom#inconsistentchainbottom silm:hasLongDescription "The InconsistentChainBottom is the lower route disagreeing with chain_top. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'chain_bottom', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
